6,Uto-Aztecan Language Family - Origins & Classification - MustGo,https://www-mustgo-com.nproxy.org/worldlanguages/uto-aztecan-language-family/,"Uto-Aztecan stock is one of the largest language groups of North and Central America in terms of population, linguistic diversity and geographic distribution. The northernmost Uto-Aztecan language, Northern Paiute, is found as far north as Oregon and Idaho.","Nahuatl, Morelos",Uto-Aztecan
7,"Aztlan Affirmed, Part VI: Uto-Aztecan Homeland?",https://readmedium.com/aztlan-affirmed-part-vi-uto-aztecan-homeland-2a3d84149412,"Southern Uto-Aztecans lived in what is now Northwest Mexico. Over the next couple of millennia, those groups spread out, their language splitting and evolving into new families. The southern branch gave rise to Tepiman, Tarahumaran, Cahita, Opatan, Corachol.","Nahuatl, Morelos",Uto-Aztecan
